% NY N342008 (August 2024): a woman's reversible tank top from Taiwan.
scenario ny_n342008 is:
% the reversible tank top is style 018085.
    the reversible tank top is an upper body garment,
        as stated in ruling NY N342008 at "018085 is a woman’s reversible tank top composed of 80 percent nylon and 20 percent spandex knit fabric".
    the reversible tank top is classified under the US tariff,
        as stated in ruling NY N342008 at "Harmonized Tariff Schedule of the United States (HTSUS)".
    the fabric construction of the reversible tank top is knitted,
        as stated in ruling NY N342008 at "percent nylon and 20 percent spandex knit fabric".
    the cut of the reversible tank top indicates women,
        as stated in ruling NY N342008 at "018085 is a woman’s reversible tank top composed of 80 percent nylon and 20 percent spandex knit fabric".
    the reversible tank top is sleeveless,
        as stated in ruling NY N342008 at "The sleeveless garment features a racer back style with a scooped front neckline".
    the reversible tank top has shoulder straps,
        as stated in ruling NY N342008 at "shoulder straps that measure 1¼ inch wide".
    the rear neckline of the reversible tank top falls below the nape of the neck,
        as stated in ruling NY N342008 at "a rear neckline that falls below the nape of the neck".
    the reversible tank top contains 80 percent of nylon,
        as stated in ruling NY N342008 at "reversible tank top composed of 80 percent nylon and 20 percent spandex knit fabric".
    the reversible tank top contains 20 percent of spandex,
        as stated in ruling NY N342008 at "of 80 percent nylon and 20 percent spandex knit fabric".
    subheading expects answers ["the subheading of the reversible tank top is 6109.90"].

% NY N348144 (January 2026): a women's knit sweater from Cambodia.
scenario ny_n348144 is:
    style 239752 is an upper body garment,
        as stated in ruling NY N348144 at "239752 is a women’s knit sweater stated to be constructed from 50 percent cotton".
    style 239752 is classified under the US tariff,
        as stated in ruling NY N348144 at "Harmonized Tariff Schedule of the United States (HTSUS)".
    the fabric construction of style 239752 is knitted,
        as stated in ruling NY N348144 at "239752 is a women’s knit sweater stated to be constructed from 50 percent cotton".
    the cut of style 239752 indicates women,
        as stated in ruling NY N348144 at "239752 is a women’s knit sweater stated to be constructed from 50 percent cotton".
    style 239752 contains 47.7 percent of cotton,
        as stated in ruling NY N348144 at "47.7 percent cotton".
    style 239752 contains 31.3 percent of polyester,
        as stated in ruling NY N348144 at "31.3 percent polyester".
    style 239752 contains 13.7 percent of nylon,
        as stated in ruling NY N348144 at "13.7 percent nylon".
    style 239752 contains 6.6 percent of elastane,
        as stated in ruling NY N348144 at "6.6 percent elastane".
    style 239752 contains 0.7 percent of metalized yarn, as stated in ruling NY N348144.
    all the yarn of style 239752 is metalized yarn,
        according to the CBP laboratory, as stated in ruling NY N348144 at "with all plies twisted together",
        because "the garment is knitted from a single eight-ply yarn with all plies, two of them metallic, twisted together".
    subheading expects answers ["the subheading of style 239752 is 6110.90"].

